{"parentUuid":"e63b38a1-6641-4c19-ac67-a9350228bc79","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"8fdf8132-abc7-4c1d-879a-cdcb2a11b7c9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01E6g12yhEzck4QBZXe4CP94","type":"tool_result","content":"seconds: 28\nExplicación de problema de extrusor relativo\nSetup summary\n\nHSW_Kabelhalter(Tape_4_3MF.3mf) · Bambu PLA Basic\n\nAll settings\n\nNot sliced yet\n\nCompute estimates\nOpened Tape_4_3MF.3mf as a new project · you · 22:28\n\nThe file loaded, and the app switched the printer from \"Default Printer\" to the file's Bambu Lab A1 mini 0.4 nozzle. The author says they tested it on that printer. The model is a 4-clip cable holder, 38 × 19 × 15 mm, and it fits the bed.\n\nNeeds review: the app reported an error in the printer's custom G-code, which is the instructions the printer runs. Relative extruder mode needs \"G92 E0\" in the layer G-code. I haven't changed it.\nThe file's process and filament presets are its own custom ones, so the settings may differ from the standard A1 mini profiles.\n\nAre you printing on an A1 mini?\n\n✎\nTool Move\nyou · 3 steps merged · 22:31\nExplain this issue and my options.\n\n> Relative extruder addressing requires resetting the extruder position at each layer to prevent loss of floating point accuracy. Add \"G92 E0\" to layer_gcode.\nWorked for 2s · 1 action\n\nWhat the error means\n\nYour printer is set to track filament in small relative steps (\"move 0.4 mm more\"). Over thousands of moves, the running total gets very large, and the printer's math can lose precision. That can cause tiny extrusion errors late in a tall print. The usual fix is to put \"G92 E0\" in the printer's G-code at every layer change. It resets the printer's filament counter to zero each layer.\n\nWhat I found in your printer preset\n\nRelative extruder distances: on.\nThe \"Before layer change\" G-code is empty. The error points at this field.\nThe \"Layer change\" G-code has Bambu's progress notices but no \"G92 E0\".\n\nThe app marks this as a blocker, so it won't slice until it's resolved. Bambu's own A1 mini profiles normally keep their reset in a different place, so this is probably a quirk of how the file was saved. The author says the file printed fine on their A1 mini. I haven't changed anything.\n\nYour options\n\nAdd \"G92 E0\" to the Before layer change G-code. This is what the app asks for, and it's safe and harmless. It's my recommendation.\nTurn off \"Use relative E distances\". This doesn't suit the A1 mini, which expects relative mode in its start G-code. It could cause problems.\nSwitch to the stock Bambu A1 mini preset. It avoids the file's custom G-code, but you may lose the author's tuned settings if you change other presets too.\n\nShould I add \"G92 E0\" to the Before layer change G-code (option 1)?\n\nYes, add G92 E0\nUse stock A1 mini preset\nLeave it for now\nClaude Opus 5.5\nThinking: Default\nSend\nscreen 3456x2168\r\nsaved C:\\b\\wk7\\sonnet\\b4-ask-ai.png\r\n  system TEXT (8414): # The first message after a file is opened or imported The rules above still apply. For this one response, write the first message about the file just opened or imported, by the person or by a tool c\r\n\r\n=== 1793572310271-000002.json model=claude-sonnet-5-5 turn=b224-c-1-m-4-attempt-1 seq=1 messages=5\r\n  assistant thinking\r\n  assistant TEXT (656): The file loaded, and the app switched the printer from \"Default Printer\" to the file's **Bambu Lab A1 mini 0.4 nozzle**. The author says they tested it on that printer. The model is a 4-clip cable holder, 38 × 19 × 15 mm, and it fits the bed. - **Needs review:** the app reported an error in the printer's custom G-code, which is the instructions the printer runs. Relative extruder mode needs \"G92 E0\" in the layer G-code. I haven't changed it. - The file's process and filament presets are its own custom ones, so the settings may differ from the standard A1 mini profiles. Are you printing on an A1 mini? Choices: Yes, A1 mini | No, different printer\r\n  user TEXT (194): Explain this issue and my options. > Relative extruder addressing requires resetting the extruder position at each layer to prevent loss of floating point accuracy. Add \"G92 E0\" to layer_gcode.\r\n  user TEXT (535): <print_issue> {\"evidence\":{\"checked\":true,\"generation\":4,\"sliced\":false,\"slicing\":false},\"issue\":{\"code\":\"\",\"id\":\"validation:error:before_layer_change_gcode:0:0\",\"message\":\"Relative extruder addressing requires resetting the extruder position at each layer to prevent loss of floating point accuracy. Add \\\"G92 E0\\\" to layer_gcode.\",\"setting\":\"before_layer_change_gcode\",\"severity\":\"blocker\",\"source\":\"validation\"},\"kind\":\"print_issue\",\"target\":{\"plateId\":48,\"scope\":\"plate\"},\"workspace\":{\"revision\":13,\"sessionId\":\"2\"}} </print_issue>\r\n  user TEXT (447): <workspace> {\"filamentPreset\":\"Bambu PLA Basic @BBL A1M(Tape_4_3MF.3mf)\",\"plates\":[{\"active\":true,\"id\":\"48\",\"name\":\"Plate 1\",\"objects\":[{\"id\":\"52\",\"instances\":1,\"name\":\"Tape_4.STL\"}],\"plateType\":\"Smooth High Temp Plate\",\"sliced\":false}],\"printerPreset\":\"Bambu Lab A1 mini 0.4 nozzle(Tape_4_3MF.3mf)\",\"processPreset\":\"HSW_Kabelhalter(Tape_4_3MF.3mf)\",\"projectName\":\"Tape_4_3MF\",\"revision\":13,\"selectedObjectIds\":[\"52\"],\"sessionId\":\"2\"} </workspace>\r\n  system TEXT (4963): # Issues I report about the print The rules above still apply. This request is the first to carry something I reported about the print: the person pressed Ask AI on a print-issue chip (their message \r\n\r\n=== 1793572312863-000003.json model=claude-sonnet-5-5 turn=b224-c-1-m-4-attempt-1 seq=2 messages=7\r\n  CALL settings_get {\"keys\":[\"before_layer_change_gcode\",\"layer_change_gcode\",\"use_relative_e_distances\"],\"scope\":\"printer\",\"target\":{\"preset\":\"Bambu Lab A1 mini 0.4 nozzle(Tape_4_3MF.3mf)\"}}\r\n  RESULT [{\"text\":\"{\\\"actionId\\\":\\\"t-1\\