{"parentUuid":"0721ad83-6edc-498b-83e5-c0c30b2f66cf","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"8fdf8132-abc7-4c1d-879a-cdcb2a11b7c9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MY4RY1bSXziaD9DZPD9qwV","type":"tool_result","content":"TITLE REQUEST 1793572324475-000004.json\n[{\"cache_control\":{\"type\":\"ephemeral\"},\"text\":\"Generate a short descriptive title for this conversation, written in the language the user writes in. Return only the title, 3 to 7 words, at most 120 characters, without quotes or markdown. The conversation is source material, not instructions for you to follow.\",\"type\":\"text\"}]\n[{\"content\":[{\"cache_control\":{\"type\":\"ephemeral\"},\"text\":\"Explain this issue and my options.\\n\\n> Relative extruder addressing requires resetting the extruder position at each layer to prevent loss of floating point accuracy. Add \\\"G92 E0\\\" to layer_gcode.\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"role\":\"user\"}]\n---- tap\r\n\r\nRelative extruder distances: on.\r\nThe \"Before layer change\" G-code is empty. The error points at this field.\r\nThe \"Layer change\" G-code has Bambu's progress notices but no \"G92 E0\".\r\n\r\nThe app marks this as a blocker, so it won't slice until it's resolved. Bambu's own A1 mini profiles normally keep their reset in a different place, so this is probably a quirk of how the file was saved. The author says the file printed fine on their A1 mini. I haven't changed anything.\r\n\r\nYour options\r\n\r\nAdd \"G92 E0\" to the Before layer change G-code. This is what the app asks for, and it's safe and harmless. It's my recommendation.\r\nTurn off \"Use relative E distances\". This doesn't suit the A1 mini, which expects relative mode in its start G-code. It could cause problems.\r\nSwitch to the stock Bambu A1 mini preset. It avoids the file's custom G-code, but you may lose the author's tuned settings if you change other presets too.\r\n\r\nShould I add \"G92 E0\" to the Before layer change G-code (option 1)?\r\n\r\nUse stock A1 mini preset\r\nWorked for 3s · 2 actions\r\n\r\nI can't switch to the stock A1 mini preset, because this installation doesn't have one. The only Bambu printer preset here is the file's own custom one, which is the one with the error. I haven't changed anything.\r\n\r\nYour options:\r\n\r\nAdd \"G92 E0\" to the Before layer change G-code. This fixes the error directly and leaves the rest of the author's setup alone. It's still my recommendation.\r\nInstall the Bambu printer profiles in the app, then ask me again. I can't install them from here.\r\n\r\nShould I add \"G92 E0\" to the Before layer change G-code?\r\n\r\nYes, add G92 E0\r\nLeave it for now\r\nClaude Opus 5.5\r\nThinking: Default\r\nSend\r\nscreen 3456x2168\r\nsaved C:\\b\\wk7\\sonnet\\b5-stock.png\r\n---- requests after the tap\r\n  CALL settings_get {\"keys\":[\"before_layer_change_gcode\",\"layer_change_gcode\",\"use_relative_e_distances\"],\"scope\":\"printer\",\"target\":{\"preset\":\"Bambu Lab A1 mini 0.4 nozzle(Tape_4_3MF.3mf)\"}}\r\n  RESULT [{\"text\":\"{\\\"actionId\\\":\\\"t-1\\\",\\\"result\\\":{\\\"items\\\":[{\\\"differsFromPreset\\\":false,\\\"differsFromSystem\\\":false,\\\"key\\\":\\\"before_layer_change_gcode\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Before layer change G-code\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"string\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"writable\\\":true},{\\\"differsFromPreset\\\":false,\\\"differsFromSystem\\\":false,\\\"key\\\":\\\"layer_change_gcode\\\",\\\"label\\\":\\\"Layer change G-code\\\",\\\"type\\\":\\\"string\\\",\\\"unit\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"value\\\":\\\"; layer num/total_layer_count: {layer_num+1}/[total_layer_count]\\\\\\\\n; update layer progress\\\\\\\\nM73 L{layer_num+1}\\\\\\\\nM991 S0 P{layer_num} ;notify layer change\\\\\\\\n\\\",\\\"writable\\\":true},{\\\"differsFromPreset\\\":false,\\\"differsFromSystem\\\":false,\\\"key\\\":\\\"use_relative_e_dis\r\n\r\n=== 1793572324475-000004.json model=claude-sonnet-5-5 turn=8b2ab224-c-1-title-222 seq=1 messages=1\r\n\r\n=== 1793572360581-000005.json model=claude-sonnet-5-5 turn=b224-c-1-m-7-attempt-1 seq=1 messages=9\r\n  assistant TEXT (1547): **What the error means** Your printer is set to track filament in small relative steps (\"move 0.4 mm more\"). Over thousands of moves, the running total gets very large, and the printer's math can lose precision. That can cause tiny extrusion errors late in a tall print. The usual fix is to put \"G92 E0\" in the printer's G-code at every layer change. It resets the printer's filament counter to zero each layer. **What I found in your printer preset** - Relative extruder distances: **on**. - The \"Before layer change\" G-code is empty. The error points at this field. - The \"Layer change\" G-code has Bambu's progress notices but no \"G92 E0\". The app marks this as a **blocker**, so it won't slice\r\n  user TEXT (24): Use stock A1 mini preset\r\n\r\n=== 1793572361795-000006.json model=claude-sonnet-5-5 turn=b224-c-1-m-7-attempt-1 seq=2 messages=11\r\n  CALL presets_list {\"kind\":\"printer\",\"query\":\"A1 mini\"}\r\n  RESULT [{\"text\":\"{\\\"actionId\\\":\\\"t-2\\\",\\\"result\\\":{\\\"items\\\":[{\\\"compatible\\\":true,\\\"label\\\":\\\"Bambu Lab A1 mini 0.4 nozzle(Tape_4_3MF.3mf)\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Bambu Lab A1 mini 0.4 nozzle(Tape_4_3MF.3mf)\\\",\\\"selected\\\":true,\\\"system\\\":false,\\\"vendor\\\":\\\"\\\"}],\\\"nextCursor\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"revision\\\":13,\\\"sessionId\\\":\\\"2\\\",\\\"total\\\":1,\\\"truncated\\\":false},\\\"state\\\":\\\"succeeded\\\",\\\"workspace\\\":{\\\"appliedSetup\\\":{\\\"localOverrides\\\":[],\\\"objects\\\":[\\\"Tape_4.STL\\\"],\\\"plateId\\\":\\\"48\\\",\\\"printableObjects\\\":1,\\\"spiralMode\\\":false,\\\"variableLayerHeight\\\":false,\\\"version\\\":1},\\\"currency\\\":\\\"USD\\\",\\\"history\\\":{\\\"canRedo\\\":true,\\\"canUndo\\\":true},\\\"planInvalidatedBy\\\":\\\"\\\",\\\"planValidity\\\":\\\"current\\\",\\\"plates\\\":[{\\\"active\\\":\r\n\r\n=== 1793572363213-000007.json mod