{"parentUuid":"43e6effe-1f7e-49d2-9251-fd4157b1bb90","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"8fdf8132-abc7-4c1d-879a-cdcb2a11b7c9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NT7XtwcbCMSHN4rWf4fgaf","type":"tool_result","content":"exited=True\r\nstarted pid 9060\r\nexited=True\r\nBambu profile: False\r\nagent settings written: anthropic / claude-sonnet-5-5\nstarted pid 11872\r\nrequests logged: 1\r\nscreen 3456x2168\r\nsaved C:\\b\\wk7\\sonnet\\c1-opened.png\r\n\"New chat\\nSetup summary\\n\\nHSW_Kabelhalter(Tape_4_3MF.3mf) · Bambu PLA Basic\\n\\nAll settings\\n\\nNot sliced yet\\n\\nCompute estimates\\nOpened Tape_4_3MF.3mf as a new project · you · 22:36\\n\\nThe file switched your printer from the Default Printer to Bambu Lab A1 mini 0.4 nozzle, a copy saved inside the file. The author says they tested it on an A1 mini. The model is a small cable holder with four clips, and it fits the bed easily.\\n\\nNeeds review: the file's printer and filament presets carry custom G-code, which is the instructions the printer runs. The app also reported an error that the layer G-code needs \\\"G92 E0\\\" (a reset of the extruder position). That may block slicing until it's fixed. I haven't reviewed the G-code yet.\\nChanged setting: \\\"Ensure vertical shell thickness\\\" was swapped to \\\"All\\\" in the file's process settings.\\n\\nAre you printing this on an A1 mini?\\n\\nYes, A1 mini\\nNo, different printer\\nReview the G-code first\\nClaude Opus 5.5\\nThinking: Default\\nSend\"\n---- question\r\nseconds: 28\nGrey Slice button and \"from the file\" printer\nSetup summary\n\nHSW_Kabelhalter(Tape_4_3MF.3mf) · Bambu PLA Basic\n\nAll settings\n\nNot sliced yet\n\nCompute estimates\nOpened Tape_4_3MF.3mf as a new project · you · 22:36\n\nThe file switched your printer from the Default Printer to Bambu Lab A1 mini 0.4 nozzle, a copy saved inside the file. The author says they tested it on an A1 mini. The model is a small cable holder with four clips, and it fits the bed easily.\n\nNeeds review: the file's printer and filament presets carry custom G-code, which is the instructions the printer runs. The app also reported an error that the layer G-code needs \"G92 E0\" (a reset of the extruder position). That may block slicing until it's fixed. I haven't reviewed the G-code yet.\nChanged setting: \"Ensure vertical shell thickness\" was swapped to \"All\" in the file's process settings.\n\nAre you printing this on an A1 mini?\n\nI'm new to this. The printer at the top says 'from the file' and the Slice button is grey. What does that mean, and what should I do?\nWorked for 6s · 3 actions\n\nWhat \"from the file\" means: the project came with its own copy of the printer, filament and print settings, and the app loaded them. The printer is the author's A1 mini setup. It isn't one of the app's built-in printer profiles, and it's the only A1 mini profile installed here. That's normal for downloaded projects.\n\nWhy Slice is grey: the file's printer settings have a conflict.\n\n\"Relative extruder distances\" is on. The printer then tracks filament feed as small step-by-step amounts.\nThe \"layer change\" G-code, which runs at the start of every layer, is missing a G92 E0 line. That line resets the extruder counter.\nWithout it, the app treats the settings as invalid and won't slice. Rounding errors could also build up over a long print.\n\nWhat I'd do: add G92 E0 to the layer change G-code, then slice. I'd add it to the end of the existing lines and leave the rest of the G-code alone. It's a small, standard fix. It does edit printer G-code that came from a downloaded file, so I'm asking first.\n\nDo you want me to make that change and then slice?\n\nYes, fix it and slice\nExplain more first\nNo, leave it\nClaude Opus 5.5\nThinking: Default\nSend\nscreen 3456x2168\r\nsaved C:\\b\\wk7\\sonnet\\c2-question.png\r\n---- requests\r\n  system TEXT (8414): # The first message after a file is opened or imported The rules above still a