{"parentUuid":"ff373809-8ae2-4a6c-a2b9-0fbded2586cc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgd1gVcWwSomNxK23SFXz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TP3hZRthgvUWAevS9F5WLy","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"C:\\Users\\guitest\\.claude\\projects\\C--src-JusPrin\\memory\\windows-baseline-2026-11-01.md","old_string":"**Why:** Saves the next Windows pass from re-diagnosing these.","new_string":"Real chat with a real model: `C:\\b\\wk7\\conf-sonnet.mjs <conf>` copies the Anthropic key from `%APPDATA%\\JusPrin2\\JusPrin2.conf` into a scratch conf and sets `model`; `s42.ps1` does a whole fresh start; `turn.mjs` taps or types and waits; `toolcalls.mjs <request-log>` lists what each request added. `wipe-key.mjs <folders>` afterwards: the app also writes `JusPrin2.conf.bak`. The picker's label ignores the conf's `model` (it said Opus 5.5 while every request's body said claude-sonnet-5-5), so read the model from the request log, never the label. Sliced G-code stays in `%TEMP%\\orcaslicer_model\\...\\Metadata\\.<pid>.0.gcode` only until the app exits.\n\n**Why:** Saves the next Windows pass from re-diagnosing these."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6232,"cache_read_input_tokens":225518,"output_tokens":721,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":164},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6232,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":721,"cache_read_input_tokens":225518,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6232,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6232},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01TP3hZRthgvUWAevS9F5WLy":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\guitest\\.claude\\projects\\C--src-JusPrin\\memory\\windows-baseline-2026-11-01.md","old_string":"**Why:** Saves the next Windows pass from re-diagnosing these.","new_string":"Real chat with a real model: `C:\\b\\wk7\\conf-sonnet.mjs <conf>` copies the Anthropic key from `%APPDATA%\\JusPrin2\\JusPrin2.conf` into a scratch conf and sets `model`; `s42.ps1` does a whole fresh start; `turn.mjs` taps or types and waits; `toolcalls.mjs <request-log>` lists what each request added. `wipe-key.mjs <folders>` afterwards: the app also writes `JusPrin2.conf.bak`. The picker's label ignores the conf's `model` (it said Opus 5.5 while every request's body said claude-sonnet-5-5), so read the model from the request log, never the label. Sliced G-code stays in `%TEMP%\\orcaslicer_model\\...\\Metadata\\.<pid>.0.gcode` only until the app exits.\n\n**Why:** Saves the next Windows pass from re-diagnosing these."}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cgd1gVJQeP1ZwEuiNPXyD","requestRef":"0545a73d-4517-4b47-8ee6-f0c2e786e4cc","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"assistant","uuid":"eefa3b5d-ec0b-4acd-b76f-96782b8a9929","timestamp":"2026-11-01T22:40:18.706Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\src\\JusPrin","sessionId":"06cfc08f-7504-4961-807f-e1d5fa2ffb14","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"jaunty-wobbling-gosling"}
{"parentUuid":"eefa3b5d-ec0b-4acd-b76f-96782b8a9929","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"8fdf8132-abc7-4c1d-879a-cdcb2a11b7c9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TP3hZRthgvUWAevS9F5WLy","type":"tool_result","content":"The file C:\\Users\\guitest\\.claude\\projects\\C--src-JusPrin\\memory\\windows-baseline-2026-11-01.md has been updated successfully."}]},"uuid":"1b5637f4-a1ca-4fbc-bcbb-e01b3e4e56ab","timestamp":"2026-11-01T22:40:18.785Z","toolUseResult":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\guitest\\.claude\\projects\\C--src-JusPrin\\memory\\windows-baseline-2026-11-01.md","oldString":"**Why:** Saves the next Windows pass from re-diagnosing these.","newString":"Real chat with a real model: `C:\\b\\wk7\\conf-sonnet.mjs <conf>` copies the Anthropic key from `%APPDATA%\\JusPrin2\\JusPrin2.conf` into a scratch conf and sets `model`; `s42.ps1` does a whole fresh start; `turn.mjs` taps or types and waits; `toolcalls.mjs <request-log>` lists what each request added. `wipe-key.mjs <folders>` afterwards: the app also writes `JusPrin2.conf.bak`. The picker's label ignores the conf's `model` (it said Opus 5.5 while every request's body said claude-sonnet-5-5), so read the model from the request log, never the label. Sliced G-code stays in `%TEMP%\\orcaslicer_model\\...\\Metadata\\.<pid>.0.gcode` only until the app exits.\n\n**Why:** Saves the next Windows pass from re-diagnosing these.","originalFile":"---\nname: windows-baseline-2026-11-01\ndescription: \"Windows results at jusprin-newui b08a307459 plus the 2026-11-01 Windows fixes: which harness and test failures remain, why, how to run the harness at the display's real scale, and how to run a real chat offline against a local stand-in model\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 06cfc08f-7504-4961-807f-e1d5fa2ffb14\n  modified: 2026-11-01T21:12:11.035Z\n---\n\nFull Windows pass on 2026-11-01 at `b08a307459` (Release, `C:\\src\\JusPrin\\build`). Scripts are in `C:\\b\\wk7`.\n\nFixed in the working tree on 2026-11-01, uncommitted when this was written (check `git log` before relying on it): the two test compile breaks, canvas overlays staying 1x above 100% (`canvas_ui_scale`), CRLF skill text, `snapshot(2.0)` drawing 1x, and the `--printer-setup` stall (`wait_for` now runs its own event loop; Preferences opened inside `wxYield` never got its web view started. Removing the yield fixed it; the inner reason is unproven).\n\nBug 3 (a Bambu 3MF on a new data folder can't slice) is waiting on Kenneth's decision as of 2026-11-01. A bare copy of the Bambu profiles is deleted at startup (`PresetUpdater::check_installed_vendor_profiles`) unless `models` in the conf names the vendor, so a lasting install has to record a model. `C:\\b\\wk7\\s32.ps1` shows the result by hand.\n\nRequest log unit tests (`tests/agent/test_provider_agent.cpp:1077`, from 9cf641098c) share a temp folder name across processes, so they fail under `ctest -j` and pass alone. Not a product fault.\n\nStill failing on Windows:\n- Default shell harness, 6 checks: `failed_autosave_is_visible`, `failed_autosave_has_plain_status_text`, `failed_autosave_blocks_project_release`, `earlier_model_version_available` (`std::filesystem::permissions` does nothing on Windows; the `UnavailableFolder` helper is the fix), and the 2 `agent_panel_columns_tile_*`.\n- `--home-live` stalls at `home_live_page_shows_online`: Home v3 draws an idle printer as `.printer-chip`, and the harness reads the old card.\n- ctest: PlaceholderParser coFloatsOrPercents segfault and `pick_attachment` previewText (CRLF in the test's own file). Workspace harness: `second_model_dropped`, `model_added_to_a_project_is_an_edit`.\n- `tests/project_prompt/test_claude_cli.py`: `claude_cli.py` hard-codes `dir=\"/tmp\"`.\n\n**The shell harness exe ignores display scale on Windows:** it has no DPI-aware manifest, so it runs at 1x even on a 200% display, and a harness pass says nothing about scaling. Set `__COMPAT_LAYER=HIGHDPIAWARE` before starting it to get the real scale (`C:\\b\\wk7\\s21.ps1`). `__COMPAT_LAYER=DPIUNAWARE` makes the DPI-aware real app run as if at 100%. With HIGHDPIAWARE, `cp_c_keyboard_selection_scrolls_into_view` fails because the panel is tall enough that its last row needs no scroll: a test assumption, not an app fault.\n\nReal chat with no provider: `C:\\b\\wk7\\mock.mjs` is a local Responses API stand-in. Start the app with `JUSPRIN_AGENT_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:8765/v1/responses` and a placeholder key in the scratch `JusPrin2.conf` (`conf-agent.mjs`: the file ends in an MD5 line, a hand edit without it is discarded). `chat.mjs` then drives the page with real typed input and wheel events over DevTools.\n\n**Why:** Saves the next Windows pass from re-diagnosing these.\n**How to apply:** Compare new failures against this list, and re-check anything here before quoting it, since fixes may have landed. See [[windows-build-machine]], [[native-ui-synthetic-input-and-capture]].\n\nThe RDP session can change display scale mid-run when Kenneth reconnects (100% to 200% on 2026-11-01). Whole-screen capture coordinates change with it, so re-read `query session` and the screen size if a click misses.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":5,"oldLines":7,"newStart":5,"newLines":7,"lines":["   node_type: memory","   type: project","   originSessionId: 06cfc08f-7504-4961-807f-e1d5fa2ffb14","-  modified: 2026-11-01T21:12:11.035Z","+  modified: 2026-11-01T22:40:18.769Z"," ---"," "," Full Windows pass on 2026-11-01 at `b08a307459` (Release, `C:\\src\\JusPrin\\build`). Scripts are in `C:\\b\\wk7`."]},{"oldStart":26,"oldLines":6,"newStart":26,"newLines":8,"lines":[" "," Real chat with no provider: `C:\\b\\wk7\\mock.mjs` is a local Responses API stand-in. Start the app with `JUSPRIN_AGENT_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:8765/v1/responses` and a placeholder key in the scratch `JusPrin2.conf` (`conf-agent.mjs`: the file ends in an MD5 line, a hand edit without it is discarded). `chat.mjs` then drives the page with real typed input and wheel events over DevTools."," ","+Real chat with a real model: `C:\\b\\wk7\\conf-sonnet.mjs <conf>` copies the Anthropic key from `%APPDATA%\\JusPrin2\\JusPrin2.conf` into a scratch conf and sets `model`; `s42.ps1` does a whole fresh start; `turn.mjs` taps or types and waits; `toolcalls.mjs <request-log>` lists what each request added. `wipe-key.mjs <folders>` afterwards: the app also writes `JusPrin2.conf.bak`. The picker's label ignores the conf's `model` (it said Opus 5.5 while every request's body said claude-sonnet-5-5), so read the model from the request log, never the label. Sliced G-code stays in `%TEMP%\\orcaslicer_model\\...\\Metadata\\.<pid>.0.gcode` only until the app exits.","+"," **Why:** Saves the next Windows pass from re-diagnosing these."," **How to apply:** Compare new failures against this list, and re-check anything here before quoting it, since fixes may have landed. See [[windows-build-machine]], [[native-ui-synthetic-input-and-capture]]."," "]}],"userModified":false,"replaceAll":false,"contentNotInModelContext":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"eefa3b5d-ec0b-4acd-b76f-96782b8a9929","permissionDecision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reasonType":"mode"},"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\src\\JusPrin","sessionId":"06cfc08f-7504-4961-807f-e1d5fa2ffb14","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"jaunty-wobbling-gosling"}
