{"type":"api-request","sessionId":"06cfc08f-7504-4961-807f-e1d5fa2ffb14","id":"44e5e262-70c4-4d49-8aad-536a1c904381","timestamp":"2026-11-01T22:40:46.742Z","version":"2.1.304","querySource":"sdk","shapeHash":"95e2999ddcbcebc7408e321dab1dfa72275ded0efcb3f64d4fd60084214868b8","params":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","betas":["claude-code-20250219","oauth-2025-04-20","interleaved-thinking-2025-05-14","thinking-token-count-2026-05-13","context-management-2025-06-27","prompt-caching-scope-2026-01-05","per-turn-control-2026-07-01","mid-conversation-tool-changes-2026-07-01","inline-tools-2026-09-15","advisor-tool-2026-03-01","advanced-tool-use-2025-11-20","mid-conversation-system-clear-at-2026-08-21","effort-2025-11-24","thinking-binding-controls-2026-08-01","thinking-display-updates-2026-08-18","extended-cache-ttl-2025-04-11","cache-diagnosis-2026-04-07","message-threads-2026-08-12"],"max_tokens":128000,"thinking":{"type":"adaptive","display":"updates"},"context_management":{"edits":[{"type":"clear_thinking_20251015","keep":"all"}]},"output_config":{"effort":"high"}},"base":"38c39829-2c09-4e88-95d5-7c2e073b0d6b","keep":55,"tail":["e0c29fd6f8aa01208f2aa0d84f4db7a01bff634d3bae6ac1f1a285ea0203218d","726c101711cc2d11e6041051d31e0e54eaf57b70eff4e803dc067802eea62a6d"],"cacheControl":[{"path":["system",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h","scope":"global"}},{"path":["system",2],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}},{"path":["messages",56,"content",1],"value":{"type":"ephemeral","ttl":"1h"}}],"requestDigest":"5ec7b48c678a2c720c94a54dc2284c7bd844d4166a7f0eddef2a137d3ac57235"}
{"parentUuid":"1266609f-f9a9-4cca-a834-de633cd1dcef","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgd1j46RtP1ResXWK9FT9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both skills can fire, but the chat doesn't explain this file well to a new user. Its first message never says Slice is blocked or what to do about it. The more serious problem is that after a bare \"Yes, A1 mini\", the model edited the printer's G-code and sliced without asking, and that turned Print on.\n\n## How it was run\n- **Runs:** I did three fresh starts, not one, because the first run never reached print-issues. That made 24 requests in total, and I didn't measure the cost. Each path ran only once, and the wording changed from run to run, so treat the replies as examples.\n- **Model:** every logged request went to `claude-sonnet-5-5`, even though the picker said \"Claude Opus 5.5\". The picker's label ignores the model saved in settings; I didn't check whether a normal setup shows the same mismatch.\n- **Agent setup:** I wrote the settings directly rather than using the setup screen, so that screen wasn't tested.\n- **Your key:** I copied the Anthropic key from this machine's JusPrin settings into the test folders. It's now removed, and a search of those folders finds no copy.\n\n## Did each skill fire?\n- **file-loaded:** it fired by itself on all three opens.\n- **print-issues:** it fired once, when I pressed Ask AI on the chip.\n    - **No chip at first:** the chip wasn't there when the file opened. \"1 print issue · 1 blocking\" appeared only after I nudged the object, so a new user sees a grey Slice button with no chip to press.\n    - **Not on a blocked slice:** when the model tried to slice and was refused, the slice-failed skill fired instead. print-issues didn't fire there, or on the clean slice that followed.\n\n## What was sent to the model\n- **On open:** the file report, the current project state, a picture of the plate and the skill's text.\n- **On Ask AI:** the `<print_issue>` block, with the error marked as a blocker, plus the skill's text.\n- **What the file report leaves out:**\n    - It doesn't say Slice is blocked; it only carries the error text. So the first replies say this \"may\" stop slicing, or don't mention slicing at all.\n    - It doesn't say which plate the file asks for, although the skill tells the model to check the plate against the file.\n    - It shows that the person has no printers set up, but no first reply used that.\n\n## Did the replies help a new user?\n- **First message:** no. All three name \"Default Printer\" and ask whether you're printing on an A1 mini. None says Slice is grey, says this isn't one of your printers, or gives a next step. They do mention \"G92 E0\", but with little or no explanation.\n- **Tapping \"Yes, A1 mini\":** the model added `G92 E0` to the printer's G-code, sliced, and offered to send the print.\n    - It also said it hadn't reviewed the file's start and end G-code, yet called it \"standard\". It had only read the layer-change settings.\n    - The slice uses the Smooth High Temp plate, but the file asks for Textured PEI. The start G-code only lowers the nozzle for Textured PEI, so someone using the plate the file asks for would miss that adjustment. The reply did ask them to check their plate.\n    - It came out at about 24 minutes and 4.8 g, against about 22 minutes and 4.6 g with the vendor installed by hand. Nothing was printed, and I didn't check whether this G-code suits a real A1 mini.\n- **Ask AI:** it explains the error reasonably and doesn't change anything, but has three problems:\n    - It says the cause is \"probably a quirk of how the file was saved\". The skill forbids supplying a cause, and the error went away in my earlier test when the vendor was installed.\n    - It calls the fix \"safe and harmless\" with nothing to back that up.\n    - It offers a \"stock A1 mini preset\" button that doesn't exist here. Pressing it was the only time the model mentioned installing the Bambu profiles, and it didn't say how.\n- **Asking in plain words:** this was the best reply. It explains \"from the file\" clearly, says why Slice is grey, and asks before editing. It still blames a conflict in the file's settings, not the missing profiles.\n\nAcross the runs the model suggested two different places for the fix: Layer change G-code and Before layer change G-code. One chat also got a Spanish title from an English message.\n\n## What this means for Bug 3\nUntil the Bambu profiles are installed, the model tends to clear the block by editing G-code. The app still doesn't treat the printer as Bambu after that edit, which is the risk the Mac notes warned about: the block clears while the G-code is still produced as non-Bambu. I inferred that from the Mac notes and didn't test it here, but it makes me more confident in installing the vendor.\n\nNo repo code changed, and nothing is committed.\n\nThe picture is `C:\\b\\wk7\\bugs-labelled\\Bug-3-Sonnet-replies.png`, and the logged requests are in `C:\\b\\wk7\\ddS`, `ddS2` and `ddS3`, under `jusprin\\request-log`.\n\n**Should a Bambu file install the Bambu vendor when it's opened?** Yes means I build it and finish the remaining checks. No means I come back with other options for Bug 3. I recommend yes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2932,"cache_read_input_tokens":235282,"output_tokens":1727,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2932,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1727,"cache_read_input_tokens":235282,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2932,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2932},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cgd1j3mqA4vZp9vYHofJV","requestRef":"44e5e262-70c4-4d49-8aad-536a1c904381","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"assistant","uuid":"35d8f8e8-c216-4c19-b14b-333a70e3ebd8","timestamp":"2026-11-01T22:41:03.517Z","advisorModel":"claude-opus-5-5","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":"high","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\src\\JusPrin","sessionId":"06cfc08f-7504-4961-807f-e1d5fa2ffb14","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"jaunty-wobbling-gosling"}
