{"parentUuid":"82f8d7ba-11a3-4e6f-a8dc-7f07296e9e88","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"ffe683db-d594-46a5-9eb8-9df5002f3bd3","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\n<tools-used-before-summary>Bash, Edit, Glob, Grep, PowerShell, Read, SendUserFile, Write, mcp__ccd_turn__update_plan, mcp__ccd_turn__wrap_up</tools-used-before-summary>\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   - Original: \"pull from remote. check the commits made in the past 7 days and understand what they are for. test these comits on this windows machine\". Then \"Compile breaks only\". Then capture and decide on bugs, and relabel the screenshots so they are readable. Then Windows-specific fixes (bug 1, CRLF skill text, 2x snapshot, --printer-setup stall): done. Then Mac results for bugs 2 and 3: Bug 2 fixed on Windows; Bug 3 hit the \"stop and ask Kenneth\" condition.\n   - Latest request (verbatim in section 6): test Bug 3's scenario with real Sonnet 5.5 (billed run approved), new data folder with no Bambu profiles, set up the agent, open Tape_4_3MF.3mf, read file-loaded and print-issues skills first, check whether each fires, what gets sent to the model, and whether its reply explains the printer from the file and the blocked Slice in words a new user can act on. No code changes. Report in plain English.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - JusPrin: long-lived fork of OrcaSlicer (C++17, wxWidgets, CMake), Agent page in WebView2 (React/Vite), `src/slic3r/GUI/JusPrin/`. Rules: AGENTS.md attribution; fork-stewardship before editing Orca-owned files; temp docs stay untracked; commit only when asked; commit trailer `Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>`; PR footer `🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)`. Kenneth wants plain-English reports, not jargon or count tables, and labelled pictures.\n   - Skills: `AgentUI/src/skills/{file-loaded,print-issues,slice-failed,project-setup-changed,calibration}/SKILL.md`. Fired in `AgentHost.cpp`: `on_file_loaded` (1577) adds a note and starts a turn; `fire_skill` (1112) attaches the plate picture and `kNoPurposeSentence`; `fire_on_new_slice_failure` (1144); `fire_print_issues` (1159) fires only if a plate has fresh `slice_warnings` or the chip was pressed (`issue_context` non-empty).\n   - `PrintIssueMonitor::compare()/rebuild()/find_validation` builds chip issues from held notifications; in practice the chip did not appear at open, only after an edit.\n   - Agent settings live in the conf section `jusprin_agent` (`anthropic_api_key`, `provider`, `model`, `enabled`, `cloud_consent`); the conf ends in an MD5 line and the app also writes `JusPrin2.conf.bak`. Request log: `<datadir>/jusprin/request-log/*.json` (no credential; picture bytes left out). `AppConfigChatModelSource` does not read the conf's `model`; picker label showed Opus 5.5 while request bodies said claude-sonnet-5-5.\n   - Print-blocking check depends on vendor lookup; the Mac notes warned `m_isBBLPrinter` has 16 uses in libslic3r, including G-code generation, so the block can clear while G-code is still produced as non-Bambu.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - No repo code changed this turn. The working tree on `jusprin-newui` at `69780c7af4` still holds the earlier uncommitted edits (16 files): CanvasIcons.hpp/.cpp (`canvas_ui_scale`), IssueOverlay.cpp, ViewportToolStrip.cpp, ToolValuePanel.cpp, CheckPrintDialog.cpp, HeaderControls.cpp, skillParser.ts, skills.test.ts, SetupCommands.cpp (Bug 2 fix), PrinterOrigin.hpp, shell_harness.cpp, print_issues_scenario.inc, check_print_scenario.inc, test_provider_live.cpp, test_shell_theme.cpp. Nothing committed.\n   - Scratch scripts in `C:\\b\\wk7`: `conf-sonnet.mjs` (copies key from main conf to scratch conf, sets model; prints no key), `s40.ps1`, `s41.ps1`, `s42.ps1` (whole fresh start), `turn.mjs` (tap/say/wait/read), `reqdump.mjs`, `toolcalls.mjs`, `key.ps1`, `wipe-key.mjs`, `s43.ps1` (picture).\n   - Evidence: `C:\\b\\wk7\\sonnet\\` (1-opened.png, 2-after-yes.png, b1..b5 pngs, c1, c2 pngs, `requests\\`, `after-model-fix.gcode`); request logs in `C:\\b\\wk7\\ddS`, `ddS2`, `ddS3` under `jusprin\\request-log`. Picture sent to user: `C:\\b\\wk7\\bugs-labelled\\Bug-3-Sonnet-replies.png`.\n   - Memory `windows-baseline-2026-11-01.md` updated with the real-model procedure.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - Picker showed \"Claude Opus 5.5\": verified via request log that all requests used `claude-sonnet-5-5`; read the model from the log, not the label. It's unverified whether a normal setup shows the same mismatch (I set `model` directly in the conf).\n   - A node one-liner failed reading `messages[1].content[0].text` because that content is a string: harmless, the data was read another way.\n   - Earlier feedback from user: screenshots must be labelled so they know which is which.\n\n5. Problem Solving (findings for the report). Each path was run once; the first replies differ between runs, so these are examples. Three fresh starts rather than one (the user approved \"this billed run\"; disclose): 24 requests total (12 + 7 + 5, including title requests). Spend not measured. Setup was by writing settings directly, not the setup screens (so setup screens untested, and I may not type keys into fields); key came from the main JusPrin settings on this machine, copied to the 3 scratch confs, then removed (3 confs cleaned, 3 `.bak` deleted, verified no file in those folders holds it). Never printed. All folders: Bambu profile absent (`system\\BBL.json` false); Bug 2 fix in this build, chip showed triangle \"Bambu Lab A1 mini · 0.4 · from the file\"; Slice grey at open.\n\n   **file-loaded:** fired on open in all 3 runs without any action. Sent: file report (load facts, printerOrigin `file_embedded`, change from \"Default Printer\", `setupPrinters: []`, fileFacts madeFor A1 mini, the three notices with auto-answers including the G92 E0 Error text, author description), workspace block (plateType Smooth High Temp Plate), plate picture, skill text plus \"Nothing is recorded about what this print is for\" sentence, system prompt, 31 tools. Not sent: anything saying Slice is greyed/blocked (report only holds the notice), any statement that the printer isn't one they set up beyond an empty list, nor the plate the file asks for (Textured PEI), though the skill says to check the plate against the file.\n   First replies: all say the printer changed to the A1 mini and ask \"Are you printing on an A1 mini?\". Two say the error \"may\" block slicing; the second doesn't mention slicing being blocked. None says Slice is grey now, none says what to do about it, none says it's not one of their printers (run 3 says \"a copy saved inside the file\"); \"G92 E0\" with little explanation. None mentions missing Bambu profiles. So: not actionable for a new user.\n\n   **print-issues:** did not fire on open: no chip on the canvas at open. Chip \"1 print issue · 1 blocking\" appeared only after I nudged the object with arrow keys (edit). Pressing it shows \"Blocks printing · Whole plate\" with the raw message and Ask AI. Pressing Ask AI fired print-issues; request carried `<print_issue>` block (severity blocker, setting before_layer_change_gcode, source validation), workspace, skill. It never fired in run 1 (slice had no warnings, slice-failed fired instead) or run 3's typed question (no extra skill).\n   Ask AI reply: explains relative extrusion and options, left project unchanged, but (a) supplies a made-up cause: \"Bambu's own A1 mini profiles normally keep their reset in a different place, so this is probably a quirk of how the file was saved\", against the skill's \"never from a cause you supply\"; the real cause per evidence is Bambu profiles not installed (with vendor recorded as installed, the error vanished in my simulation); (b) \"safe and harmless\" unsupported; (c) offers \"Use stock A1 mini preset\" as a button, which doesn't exist; tapping it, model ran presets_list, said it can't, and suggested \"Install the Bambu printer profiles in the app, then ask me again. I can't install them from here.\" (closest to the real fix, no how-to, no Bambu profile got installed); (d) chat title came out in Spanish (\"Explicación de problema de extrusor relativo\") from an English message (seen in 1 of 3 runs); other titles were English.\n\n   **Run 1, tapped only \"Yes, A1 mini\":** model read settings, called `slice_start` (refused; slice-failed skill fired), then with no question to the person added `G92 E0` to the end of `layer_change_gcode` via settings_preview_patch/settings_apply_patch, sliced, and offered to open the send dialog. Print button became active. System prompt says \"Do what the person asked, no more\"; the person only confirmed which printer. It reported the change plainly and the card shows \"1 setting changed\" and \"Layer change G-code 4 lines → 5 lines\", not saved to the preset. It said \"It's the standard A1 mini start and end G-code\" in the same breath as saying it hadn't reviewed it; its calls only read layer-change fields. Result \"The slice is clean\", ~24 min, 4.8 g, $0.12. It asked to confirm the plate is Smooth High Temp but didn't know the file asks for Textured PEI. G-code: `curr_bed_type = High Temp Plate`; the start G-code applies `G29.1 Z-0.02` only for Textured PEI, so on the plate the file wants that adjustment is skipped. Simulation with vendor earlier: about 22 min, 4.6 g on Textured PEI. Not checked: whether this G-code is right for a real A1 mini (Mac warning about non-Bambu generation stands); no comparison G-code; nothing printed; no printer connected. Inference (mark as such): the model can clear the block by editing G-code, which is exactly what the Mac notes warned about.\n   Fix location varied: run 1 and run 3 say layer change G-code; Ask AI recommended Before layer change G-code; only run 1's location was tried (slice passed).\n\n   **Run 3, typed question** \"I'm new to this. The printer at the top says 'from the file' and the Slice button is grey. What does that mean, and what should I do?\": best reply. Explains \"from the file\" as the project's own copy, not a built-in profile, the only A1 mini profile here; explains why grey; recommends adding G92 E0; explicitly asks first (\"It does edit printer G-code that came from a downloaded file, so I'm asking first\") with buttons. Still blames \"the file's printer settings have a conflict\", not missing profiles; \"That's normal for downloaded projects\" unverified; \"It isn't one of your printers\" not stated exactly. One tool call failed on missing target then retried fine.\n\n   Side finding: picker label says \"Claude Opus 5.5\" while requests went to Sonnet 5.5.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - \"pull from remote. check the commits made in the past 7 days and understand what they are for. test these comits on this windows machine\"\n   - \"Compile breaks only\"\n   - \"Capture The screenshot for the bugs that you found, and now decide if we need to fix them.\"\n   - \"You need to reorganize your screenshot so that I know which is which. I look at your screenshot, I'm like, they're fine.\"\n   - \"Bugs 2 and 3 are going to a Mac agent to check. Focus here on the problems that are probably Windows-specific: bug 1 (print issues cut off above 100% scale), plus the Windows-side test problems. Those are the CRLF skill text, the 2x snapshot pixel checks, and the --printer-setup stall. Don't work on bugs 2 and 3 until the Mac result is back.\"\n   - Mac results message: both bugs reproduce on macOS; suggested Bug 2 fix (origin from selected preset) and Bug 3 hypothesis (install vendor before file presets load, from JusPrin-owned code). \"Don't do these: Don't widen get_current_vendor_type or is_bbl_vendor... Don't just remove the rule or add an exemption to it. m_isBBLPrinter has 16 uses in libslic3r, including G-code generation, so the block would clear while the G-code is still produced as non-Bambu.\" \"Stop and ask Kenneth if this can't be a small change, or if installing the vendor changes anything a person would notice.\" \"Check that the Bambu printers don't start appearing as printers the person set up.\" \"The two fixes are independent.\" \"Follow AGENTS.md, including agent-docs/jusprin/fork-stewardship.md before editing any OrcaSlicer-owned file.\" Procedure: reproduce in Test A; after fixes check chip, menu, Slice active, error gone, slice finishes; inspect G-code against Test B; rerun Test B and open a non-Bambu file; ask for macOS retest. Upstream note: \"don't claim OrcaSlicer shows this bug.\"\n   - \"Test Bug 3's scenario with a real model, Sonnet 5.5 (claude-sonnet-5-5). I approve this billed run. Use a new data folder with no Bambu profiles, set up the agent, and open Tape_4_3MF.3mf. Read the file-loaded and print-issues skills first. Then check whether each one fires, what gets sent to the model, and whether its reply explains the printer from the file and the blocked Slice in words a new user can act on. Don't change any code. Report what happened in plain English.\"\n   - Credential handling (from memory, still in force): the main conf holds a real Anthropic key: \"never print or publish the conf, and delete copies afterwards.\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Write the closing report for the real-model test (not yet written).\n   - Still awaiting Kenneth's decisions from earlier: whether a Bambu file should install the Bambu vendor on open (no Bug 3 code until answered; if yes, then G-code comparison, Test B rerun, non-Bambu file check, timing), and whether to commit the fixes now or wait for the Mac retest (nothing committed).\n   - macOS retest needed for Bug 2 fix, canvas scale change, new `wait_for`.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   All test work is done. App closed, key copies removed, picture `Bug-3-Sonnet-replies.png` sent, `wrap_up` called with the question \"Should a Bambu file install the Bambu vendor when it's opened?\". The tool result said: \"The user is working over Remote Control and may not see the next-step box. Do not call wrap_up again this turn... Write your closing message now, as the last thing you say this turn, as if there were no box: what you did and anything that failed or is unverified, no next steps, and only what you need from them to go on, as a question with its choices.\"\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write the closing message in plain English, no further tools: lead with the verdict (file-loaded fires on open; print-issues fires only through Ask AI, and the chip appears only after an edit; the first reply doesn't tell a new user Slice is blocked or what to do; a direct question gets a good answer; a bare \"Yes, A1 mini\" led the model to edit printer G-code and slice unasked, with Print active). Then what was sent, the three paths, the wrong claims (made-up cause, nonexistent stock preset option, \"standard\" G-code unreviewed, plate mismatch, Spanish title), the Opus label, and what wasn't checked; disclose three fresh starts, 24 requests, spend unmeasured, key source and removal, settings written directly rather than through setup screens, no code changed. End by asking the only question needed: should a Bambu file install the Bambu vendor when it's opened (yes, build it / no, come back with other options), and whether to commit now or wait for the Mac retest. Do not start Bug 3 code or commit until answered.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: C:\\Users\\guitest\\.claude\\projects\\C--src-JusPrin\\06cfc08f-7504-4961-807f-e1d5fa2ffb14.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened.\n\nThe messages after this summary are the most recent messages from before compaction, kept verbatim. The summary was written without seeing them, so something it says has not happened yet may already have happened in them."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"d6d22ad6-499c-48cf-8ae7-8b9cb3f7c9ce","timestamp":"2026-11-01T23:35:37.933Z","turnPosition":{"promptIndex":6,"turnIndex":15},"turnOrigin":"human","summarizedTurnPromptUuids":["769385fb-2ebb-495d-99f3-ab35288a3ee2"],"userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\src\\JusPrin","sessionId":"06cfc08f-7504-4961-807f-e1d5fa2ffb14","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"jaunty-wobbling-gosling"}
{"parentUuid":"d6d22ad6-499c-48cf-8ae7-8b9cb3f7c9ce","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"C:\\Users\\guitest\\.claude\\projects\\C--src-JusPrin\\memory\\windows-baseline-2026-11-01.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\guitest\\.claude\\projects\\C--src-JusPrin\\memory\\windows-baseline-2026-11-01.md","content":"---\nname: windows-baseline-2026-11-01\ndescription: \"Windows results at jusprin-newui b08a307459 plus the 2026-11-01 Windows fixes: which harness and test failures remain, why, how to run the harness at the display's real scale, and how to run a real chat offline against a local stand-in model\"\nmetadata:\n  node_type: memory\n  type: project\n  originSessionId: 06cfc08f-7504-4961-807f-e1d5fa2ffb14\n  modified: 2026-11-01T22:40:18.769Z\n---\n\nFull Windows pass on 2026-11-01 at `b08a307459` (Release, `C:\\src\\JusPrin\\build`). Scripts are in `C:\\b\\wk7`.\n\nFixed in the working tree on 2026-11-01, uncommitted when this was written (check `git log` before relying on it): the two test compile breaks, canvas overlays staying 1x above 100% (`canvas_ui_scale`), CRLF skill text, `snapshot(2.0)` drawing 1x, and the `--printer-setup` stall (`wait_for` now runs its own event loop; Preferences opened inside `wxYield` never got its web view started. Removing the yield fixed it; the inner reason is unproven).\n\nBug 3 (a Bambu 3MF on a new data folder can't slice) is waiting on Kenneth's decision as of 2026-11-01. A bare copy of the Bambu profiles is deleted at startup (`PresetUpdater::check_installed_vendor_profiles`) unless `models` in the conf names the vendor, so a lasting install has to record a model. `C:\\b\\wk7\\s32.ps1` shows the result by hand.\n\nRequest log unit tests (`tests/agent/test_provider_agent.cpp:1077`, from 9cf641098c) share a temp folder name across processes, so they fail under `ctest -j` and pass alone. Not a product fault.\n\nStill failing on Windows:\n- Default shell harness, 6 checks: `failed_autosave_is_visible`, `failed_autosave_has_plain_status_text`, `failed_autosave_blocks_project_release`, `earlier_model_version_available` (`std::filesystem::permissions` does nothing on Windows; the `UnavailableFolder` helper is the fix), and the 2 `agent_panel_columns_tile_*`.\n- `--home-live` stalls at `home_live_page_shows_online`: Home v3 draws an idle printer as `.printer-chip`, and the harness reads the old card.\n- ctest: PlaceholderParser coFloatsOrPercents segfault and `pick_attachment` previewText (CRLF in the test's own file). Workspace harness: `second_model_dropped`, `model_added_to_a_project_is_an_edit`.\n- `tests/project_prompt/test_claude_cli.py`: `claude_cli.py` hard-codes `dir=\"/tmp\"`.\n\n**The shell harness exe ignores display scale on Windows:** it has no DPI-aware manifest, so it runs at 1x even on a 200% display, and a harness pass says nothing about scaling. Set `__COMPAT_LAYER=HIGHDPIAWARE` before starting it to get the real scale (`C:\\b\\wk7\\s21.ps1`). `__COMPAT_LAYER=DPIUNAWARE` makes the DPI-aware real app run as if at 100%. With HIGHDPIAWARE, `cp_c_keyboard_selection_scrolls_into_view` fails because the panel is tall enough that its last row needs no scroll: a test assumption, not an app fault.\n\nReal chat with no provider: `C:\\b\\wk7\\mock.mjs` is a local Responses API stand-in. Start the app with `JUSPRIN_AGENT_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:8765/v1/responses` and a placeholder key in the scratch `JusPrin2.conf` (`conf-agent.mjs`: the file ends in an MD5 line, a hand edit without it is discarded). `chat.mjs` then drives the page with real typed input and wheel events over DevTools.\n\nReal chat with a real model: `C:\\b\\wk7\\conf-sonnet.mjs <conf>` copies the Anthropic key from `%APPDATA%\\JusPrin2\\JusPrin2.conf` into a scratch conf and sets `model`; `s42.ps1` does a whole fresh start; `turn.mjs` taps or types and waits; `toolcalls.mjs <request-log>` lists what each request added. `wipe-key.mjs <folders>` afterwards: the app also writes `JusPrin2.conf.bak`. The picker's label ignores the conf's `model` (it said Opus 5.5 while every request's body said claude-sonnet-5-5), so read the model from the request log, never the label. Sliced G-code stays in `%TEMP%\\orcaslicer_model\\...\\Metadata\\.<pid>.0.gcode` only until the app exits.\n\n**Why:** Saves the next Windows pass from re-diagnosing these.\n**How to apply:** Compare new failures against this list, and re-check anything here before quoting it, since fixes may have landed. See [[windows-build-machine]], [[native-ui-synthetic-input-and-capture]].\n\nThe RDP session can change display scale mid-run when Kenneth reconnects (100% to 200% on 2026-11-01). Whole-screen capture coordinates change with it, so re-read `query session` and the screen size if a click misses.\n","numLines":35,"startLine":1,"totalLines":35}},"displayPath":"..\\..\\Users\\guitest\\.claude\\projects\\C--src-JusPrin\\memory\\windows-baseline-2026-11-01.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ec300909-b82f-4fba-b0bd-6c1bad917447","timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:21:50.722Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"C:\\\\Users\\\\guitest\\\\.claude\\\\projects\\\\C--src-JusPrin\\\\memory\\\\windows-baseline-2026-11-01.md\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t---\n2\tname: windows-baseline-2026-11-01\n3\tdescription: \"Windows results at jusprin-newui b08a307459 plus the 2026-11-01 Windows fixes: which harness and test failures remain, why, how to run the harness at the display's real scale, and how to run a real chat offline against a local stand-in model\"\n4\tmetadata:\n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: project\n7\t  originSessionId: 06cfc08f-7504-4961-807f-e1d5fa2ffb14\n8\t  modified: 2026-11-01T22:40:18.769Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tFull Windows pass on 2026-11-01 at `b08a307459` (Release, `C:\\src\\JusPrin\\build`). Scripts are in `C:\\b\\wk7`.\n12\t\n13\tFixed in the working tree on 2026-11-01, uncommitted when this was written (check `git log` before relying on it): the two test compile breaks, canvas overlays staying 1x above 100% (`canvas_ui_scale`), CRLF skill text, `snapshot(2.0)` drawing 1x, and the `--printer-setup` stall (`wait_for` now runs its own event loop; Preferences opened inside `wxYield` never got its web view started. Removing the yield fixed it; the inner reason is unproven).\n14\t\n15\tBug 3 (a Bambu 3MF on a new data folder can't slice) is waiting on Kenneth's decision as of 2026-11-01. A bare copy of the Bambu profiles is deleted at startup (`PresetUpdater::check_installed_vendor_profiles`) unless `models` in the conf names the vendor, so a lasting install has to record a model. `C:\\b\\wk7\\s32.ps1` shows the result by hand.\n16\t\n17\tRequest log unit tests (`tests/agent/test_provider_agent.cpp:1077`, from 9cf641098c) share a temp folder name across processes, so they fail under `ctest -j` and pass alone. Not a product fault.\n18\t\n19\tStill failing on Windows:\n20\t- Default shell harness, 6 checks: `failed_autosave_is_visible`, `failed_autosave_has_plain_status_text`, `failed_autosave_blocks_project_release`, `earlier_model_version_available` (`std::filesystem::permissions` does nothing on Windows; the `UnavailableFolder` helper is the fix), and the 2 `agent_panel_columns_tile_*`.\n21\t- `--home-live` stalls at `home_live_page_shows_online`: Home v3 draws an idle printer as `.printer-chip`, and the harness reads the old card.\n22\t- ctest: PlaceholderParser coFloatsOrPercents segfault and `pick_attachment` previewText (CRLF in the test's own file). Workspace harness: `second_model_dropped`, `model_added_to_a_project_is_an_edit`.\n23\t- `tests/project_prompt/test_claude_cli.py`: `claude_cli.py` hard-codes `dir=\"/tmp\"`.\n24\t\n25\t**The shell harness exe ignores display scale on Windows:** it has no DPI-aware manifest, so it runs at 1x even on a 200% display, and a harness pass says nothing about scaling. Set `__COMPAT_LAYER=HIGHDPIAWARE` before starting it to get the real scale (`C:\\b\\wk7\\s21.ps1`). `__COMPAT_LAYER=DPIUNAWARE` makes the DPI-aware real app run as if at 100%. With HIGHDPIAWARE, `cp_c_keyboard_selection_scrolls_into_view` fails because the panel is tall enough that its last row needs no scroll: a test assumption, not an app fault.\n26\t\n27\tReal chat with no provider: `C:\\b\\wk7\\mock.mjs` is a local Responses API stand-in. Start the app with `JUSPRIN_AGENT_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:8765/v1/responses` and a placeholder key in the scratch `JusPrin2.conf` (`conf-agent.mjs`: the file ends in an MD5 line, a hand edit without it is discarded). `chat.mjs` then drives the page with real typed input and wheel events over DevTools.\n28\t\n29\tReal chat with a real model: `C:\\b\\wk7\\conf-sonnet.mjs <conf>` copies the Anthropic key from `%APPDATA%\\JusPrin2\\JusPrin2.conf` into a scratch conf and sets `model`; `s42.ps1` does a whole fresh start; `turn.mjs` taps or types and waits; `toolcalls.mjs <request-log>` lists what each request added. `wipe-key.mjs <folders>` afterwards: the app also writes `JusPrin2.conf.bak`. The picker's label ignores the conf's `model` (it said Opus 5.5 while every request's body said claude-sonnet-5-5), so read the model from the request log, never the label. Sliced G-code stays in `%TEMP%\\orcaslicer_model\\...\\Metadata\\.<pid>.0.gcode` only until the app exits.\n30\t\n31\t**Why:** Saves the next Windows pass from re-diagnosing these.\n32\t**How to apply:** Compare new failures against this list, and re-check anything here before quoting it, since fixes may have landed. See [[windows-build-machine]], [[native-ui-synthetic-input-and-capture]].\n33\t\n34\tThe RDP session can change display scale mid-run when Kenneth reconnects (100% to 200% on 2026-11-01). Whole-screen capture coordinates change with it, so re-read `query session` and the screen size if a click misses.\n35\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\src\\JusPrin","sessionId":"06cfc08f-7504-4961-807f-e1d5fa2ffb14","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"jaunty-wobbling-gosling"}
{"parentUuid":"ec300909-b82f-4fba-b0bd-6c1bad917447","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"C:\\b\\wk7\\s43.ps1","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\b\\wk7\\s43.ps1","content":"# Labelled picture of the three real-model outcomes.\nAdd-Type -AssemblyName System.Drawing\n$red = [System.Drawing.Color]::FromArgb(214, 40, 40); $amber = [System.Drawing.Color]::FromArgb(176, 110, 0); $green = [System.Drawing.Color]::FromArgb(30, 130, 76)\n$ink = [System.Drawing.Color]::FromArgb(25, 25, 30); $grey = [System.Drawing.Color]::FromArgb(80, 80, 90)\n$title = New-Object System.Drawing.Font 'Segoe UI Semibold', 25\n$body = New-Object System.Drawing.Font 'Segoe UI', 16\n$tag = New-Object System.Drawing.Font 'Segoe UI Semibold', 15\n$scale = 0.56\n$cropX = 2590; $cropW = 866; $cropY = 80; $cropH = 2010\n$panels = @(\n  @{ F = 'C:\\b\\wk7\\sonnet\\2-after-yes.png'; T = \"1. TAPPED ONLY `\"YES, A1 MINI`\"`nIt edited the G-code, sliced, offered to send. Never asked.\"; Col = $red; X = 30 },\n  @{ F = 'C:\\b\\wk7\\sonnet\\b4-ask-ai.png'; T = \"2. PRESSED ASK AI ON THE CHIP`nGives a made-up cause. One option doesn't exist.\"; Col = $amber; X = 530 },\n  @{ F = 'C:\\b\\wk7\\sonnet\\c2-question.png'; T = \"3. ASKED IN PLAIN WORDS`nBest reply, and it asks first. Blames the file, not missing profiles.\"; Col = $green; X = 1030 }\n)\n$w = [int]($cropW * $scale)\n$bmp = New-Object System.Drawing.Bitmap 1520, 1370\n$g = [System.Drawing.Graphics]::FromImage($bmp)\n$g.Clear([System.Drawing.Color]::White); $g.SmoothingMode = 'AntiAlias'; $g.TextRenderingHint = 'AntiAliasGridFit'; $g.InterpolationMode = 'HighQualityBicubic'\n$g.DrawString('Sonnet 5.5 on the Bambu file: what the chat said, three ways in', $title, (New-Object System.Drawing.SolidBrush $ink), 30, 18)\n$g.DrawString('Same 3MF, a brand-new data folder each time, no Bambu profiles, the real app on Windows.', $body, (New-Object System.Drawing.SolidBrush $grey), 30, 70)\nforeach ($p in $panels) {\n    $img = [System.Drawing.Bitmap]::FromFile($p.F)\n    $g.FillRectangle((New-Object System.Drawing.SolidBrush $p.Col), $p.X, 112, $w, 82)\n    $g.DrawString($p.T, $tag, [System.Drawing.Brushes]::White, (New-Object System.Drawing.RectangleF ($p.X + 8), 116, ($w - 12), 78))\n    $g.DrawImage($img, (New-Object System.Drawing.Rectangle $p.X, 200, $w, ([int]($cropH * $scale))), (New-Object System.Drawing.Rectangle $cropX, $cropY, $cropW, $cropH), 'Pixel')\n    $g.DrawRectangle((New-Object System.Drawing.Pen ([System.Drawing.Color]::FromArgb(200,200,205))), $p.X, 200, $w, ([int]($cropH * $scale)))\n    $img.Dispose()\n}\n$bmp.Save('C:\\b\\wk7\\bugs-labelled\\Bug-3-Sonnet-replies.png'); $g.Dispose(); $bmp.Dispose()\n'picture saved'\n","numLines":31,"startLine":1,"totalLines":31}},"displayPath":"..\\..\\b\\wk7\\s43.ps1"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"1c6ecb24-81bf-4fbc-9d8d-ac8465327e17","timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:21:50.722Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"C:\\\\b\\\\wk7\\\\s43.ps1\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t# Labelled picture of the three real-model outcomes.\n2\tAdd-Type -AssemblyName System.Drawing\n3\t$red = [System.Drawing.Color]::FromArgb(214, 40, 40); $amber = [System.Drawing.Color]::FromArgb(176, 110, 0); $green = [System.Drawing.Color]::FromArgb(30, 130, 76)\n4\t$ink = [System.Drawing.Color]::FromArgb(25, 25, 30); $grey = [System.Drawing.Color]::FromArgb(80, 80, 90)\n5\t$title = New-Object System.Drawing.Font 'Segoe UI Semibold', 25\n6\t$body = New-Object System.Drawing.Font 'Segoe UI', 16\n7\t$tag = New-Object System.Drawing.Font 'Segoe UI Semibold', 15\n8\t$scale = 0.56\n9\t$cropX = 2590; $cropW = 866; $cropY = 80; $cropH = 2010\n10\t$panels = @(\n11\t  @{ F = 'C:\\b\\wk7\\sonnet\\2-after-yes.png'; T = \"1. TAPPED ONLY `\"YES, A1 MINI`\"`nIt edited the G-code, sliced, offered to send. Never asked.\"; Col = $red; X = 30 },\n12\t  @{ F = 'C:\\b\\wk7\\sonnet\\b4-ask-ai.png'; T = \"2. PRESSED ASK AI ON THE CHIP`nGives a made-up cause. One option doesn't exist.\"; Col = $amber; X = 530 },\n13\t  @{ F = 'C:\\b\\wk7\\sonnet\\c2-question.png'; T = \"3. ASKED IN PLAIN WORDS`nBest reply, and it asks first. Blames the file, not missing profiles.\"; Col = $green; X = 1030 }\n14\t)\n15\t$w = [int]($cropW * $scale)\n16\t$bmp = New-Object System.Drawing.Bitmap 1520, 1370\n17\t$g = [System.Drawing.Graphics]::FromImage($bmp)\n18\t$g.Clear([System.Drawing.Color]::White); $g.SmoothingMode = 'AntiAlias'; $g.TextRenderingHint = 'AntiAliasGridFit'; $g.InterpolationMode = 'HighQualityBicubic'\n19\t$g.DrawString('Sonnet 5.5 on the Bambu file: what the chat said, three ways in', $title, (New-Object System.Drawing.SolidBrush $ink), 30, 18)\n20\t$g.DrawString('Same 3MF, a brand-new data folder each time, no Bambu profiles, the real app on Windows.', $body, (New-Object System.Drawing.SolidBrush $grey), 30, 70)\n21\tforeach ($p in $panels) {\n22\t    $img = [System.Drawing.Bitmap]::FromFile($p.F)\n23\t    $g.FillRectangle((New-Object System.Drawing.SolidBrush $p.Col), $p.X, 112, $w, 82)\n24\t    $g.DrawString($p.T, $tag, [System.Drawing.Brushes]::White, (New-Object System.Drawing.RectangleF ($p.X + 8), 116, ($w - 12), 78))\n25\t    $g.DrawImage($img, (New-Object System.Drawing.Rectangle $p.X, 200, $w, ([int]($cropH * $scale))), (New-Object System.Drawing.Rectangle $cropX, $cropY, $cropW, $cropH), 'Pixel')\n26\t    $g.DrawRectangle((New-Object System.Drawing.Pen ([System.Drawing.Color]::FromArgb(200,200,205))), $p.X, 200, $w, ([int]($cropH * $scale)))\n27\t    $img.Dispose()\n28\t}\n29\t$bmp.Save('C:\\b\\wk7\\bugs-labelled\\Bug-3-Sonnet-replies.png'); $g.Dispose(); $bmp.Dispose()\n30\t'picture saved'\n31\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\src\\JusPrin","sessionId":"06cfc08f-7504-4961-807f-e1d5fa2ffb14","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"jaunty-wobbling-gosling"}
{"parentUuid":"1c6ecb24-81bf-4fbc-9d8d-ac8465327e17","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"C:\\b\\wk7\\wipe-key.mjs","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\b\\wk7\\wipe-key.mjs","content":"// Removes every copy of the Anthropic key from the scratch data folders, and reports any file still holding it. Prints no key.\nimport { readFileSync, readdirSync, statSync, writeFileSync, rmSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { createHash } from 'node:crypto';\nimport { join } from 'node:path';\nconst main = readFileSync(`${process.env.APPDATA}/JusPrin2/JusPrin2.conf`, 'latin1');\nconst key = JSON.parse(main.slice(0, main.lastIndexOf('#'))).jusprin_agent.anthropic_api_key;\nconst walk = (d) => readdirSync(d).flatMap((n) => { const p = join(d, n); const s = statSync(p); return s.isDirectory() ? walk(p) : s.size < 50e6 ? [p] : []; });\nconst holding = (d) => walk(d).filter((p) => readFileSync(p, 'latin1').includes(key));\nfor (const d of process.argv.slice(2)) {\n  for (const p of holding(d)) {\n    if (p.endsWith('JusPrin2.conf')) {\n      const raw = readFileSync(p, 'latin1');\n      const conf = JSON.parse(raw.slice(0, raw.lastIndexOf('#')));\n      delete conf.jusprin_agent;\n      const text = JSON.stringify(conf, null, '\\t') + '\\n';\n      writeFileSync(p, text + `# MD5 checksum ${createHash('md5').update(text, 'latin1').digest('hex').toUpperCase()}\\n`, 'latin1');\n      console.log('key removed from', p);\n    } else {\n      rmSync(p);\n      console.log('deleted copy', p);\n    }\n  }\n  console.log(d, 'files still holding the key:', holding(d).length);\n}\n","numLines":25,"startLine":1,"totalLines":25}},"displayPath":"..\\..\\b\\wk7\\wipe-key.mjs"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"3ec371d8-8a8b-4886-9f9c-d7eebe172115","timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:21:50.722Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"C:\\\\b\\\\wk7\\\\wipe-key.mjs\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\t// Removes every copy of the Anthropic key from the scratch data folders, and reports any file still holding it. Prints no key.\n2\timport { readFileSync, readdirSync, statSync, writeFileSync, rmSync } from 'node:fs';\n3\timport { createHash } from 'node:crypto';\n4\timport { join } from 'node:path';\n5\tconst main = readFileSync(`${process.env.APPDATA}/JusPrin2/JusPrin2.conf`, 'latin1');\n6\tconst key = JSON.parse(main.slice(0, main.lastIndexOf('#'))).jusprin_agent.anthropic_api_key;\n7\tconst walk = (d) => readdirSync(d).flatMap((n) => { const p = join(d, n); const s = statSync(p); return s.isDirectory() ? walk(p) : s.size < 50e6 ? [p] : []; });\n8\tconst holding = (d) => walk(d).filter((p) => readFileSync(p, 'latin1').includes(key));\n9\tfor (const d of process.argv.slice(2)) {\n10\t  for (const p of holding(d)) {\n11\t    if (p.endsWith('JusPrin2.conf')) {\n12\t      const raw = readFileSync(p, 'latin1');\n13\t      const conf = JSON.parse(raw.slice(0, raw.lastIndexOf('#')));\n14\t      delete conf.jusprin_agent;\n15\t      const text = JSON.stringify(conf, null, '\\t') + '\\n';\n16\t      writeFileSync(p, text + `# MD5 checksum ${createHash('md5').update(text, 'latin1').digest('hex').toUpperCase()}\\n`, 'latin1');\n17\t      console.log('key removed from', p);\n18\t    } else {\n19\t      rmSync(p);\n20\t      console.log('deleted copy', p);\n21\t    }\n22\t  }\n23\t  console.log(d, 'files still holding the key:', holding(d).length);\n24\t}\n25\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\src\\JusPrin","sessionId":"06cfc08f-7504-4961-807f-e1d5fa2ffb14","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"jaunty-wobbling-gosling"}
{"parentUuid":"3ec371d8-8a8b-4886-9f9c-d7eebe172115","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"C:\\b\\wk7\\key.ps1","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\b\\wk7\\key.ps1","content":"param([byte]$Vk, [int]$Times = 1, [switch]$Extended)\n# Presses one key with real keyboard events; arrows need the extended flag.\nAdd-Type @\"\nusing System; using System.Runtime.InteropServices;\npublic static class K9 { [DllImport(\"user32.dll\")] public static extern void keybd_event(byte v, byte s, uint f, UIntPtr e); }\n\"@\n$f = [uint32]$(if ($Extended) { 1 } else { 0 })\nfor ($i = 0; $i -lt $Times; $i++) {\n  [K9]::keybd_event($Vk, 0, $f, [UIntPtr]::Zero); Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 40\n  [K9]::keybd_event($Vk, 0, $f -bor 2, [UIntPtr]::Zero); Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 120\n}\n","numLines":12,"startLine":1,"totalLines":12}},"displayPath":"..\\..\\b\\wk7\\key.ps1"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"56190d8b-46be-4979-adcf-6bca6a71b90f","timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:21:50.722Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nCalled the Read tool with the following input: {\"file_path\":\"C:\\\\b\\\\wk7\\\\key.ps1\"}\n</system-reminder>"},{"content":"<system-reminder>\nResult of calling the Read tool:\n1\tparam([byte]$Vk, [int]$Times = 1, [switch]$Extended)\n2\t# Presses one key with real keyboard events; arrows need the extended flag.\n3\tAdd-Type @\"\n4\tusing System; using System.Runtime.InteropServices;\n5\tpublic static class K9 { [DllImport(\"user32.dll\")] public static extern void keybd_event(byte v, byte s, uint f, UIntPtr e); }\n6\t\"@\n7\t$f = [uint32]$(if ($Extended) { 1 } else { 0 })\n8\tfor ($i = 0; $i -lt $Times; $i++) {\n9\t  [K9]::keybd_event($Vk, 0, $f, [UIntPtr]::Zero); Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 40\n10\t  [K9]::keybd_event($Vk, 0, $f -bor 2, [UIntPtr]::Zero); Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 120\n11\t}\n12\t\n</system-reminder>"}],"renderedRole":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"claude-desktop","cwd":"C:\\src\\JusPrin","sessionId":"06cfc08f-7504-4961-807f-e1d5fa2ffb14","version":"2.1.304","gitBranch":"jusprin-newui","slug":"jaunty-wobbling-gosling"}
{"parentUuid":"56190d8b-46be-4979-adcf-6bca6a71b90f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"C:\\b\\wk7\\s42.ps1","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\b\\wk7\\s42.ps1","content":"# Real-model test, second pass: same fresh start in its own folder, stop after the first reply.\nparam([string]$DataDir = 'C:\\b\\wk7\\ddS2', [string]$Shot = 'C:\\b\\wk7\\sonnet\\b1-opened.png')\n$env:PATH=\"C:\\Users\\guitest\\.local\\node-v24.21.0-win-x64;$env:PATH\"\nif (Test-Path $DataDir) { Remove-Item $DataDir -Recurse -Force }\n& C:\\b\\wk7\\launch.ps1 -DataDir $DataDir\n$start=Get-Date; do { Start-Sleep -Seconds 4; $l = node C:\\b\\wk7\\cdp.mjs list 2>$null } while(($l -notmatch 'agent/index') -and ((Get-Date)-$start).TotalSeconds -lt 150)\nStart-Sleep -Seconds 12\n$p = Get-Process orca-slicer; $p.CloseMainWindow() | Out-Null; \"exited=\" + $p.WaitForExit(40000)\n\"Bambu profile: \" + (Test-Path \"$DataDir\\system\\BBL.json\")\nnode C:\\b\\wk7\\conf-sonnet.mjs \"$DataDir\\JusPrin2.conf\"\n& C:\\b\\wk7\\launch.ps1 -DataDir $DataDir -Files @('C:\\b\\wk7\\Tape_4_3MF.3mf')\n$start=Get-Date; do { Start-Sleep -Seconds 4; $l = node C:\\b\\wk7\\cdp.mjs list 2>$null } while(($l -notmatch 'agent/index') -and ((Get-Date)-$start).TotalSeconds -lt 150)\n& C:\\b\\wk7\\max.ps1\n$start=Get-Date\ndo {\n  Start-Sleep -Seconds 6\n  $n = (Get-ChildItem \"$DataDir\\jusprin\\request-log\" -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Measure-Object).Count\n  $t = node C:\\b\\wk7\\cdp.mjs eval 'agent/index.html' \"document.body.innerText\" 2>$null\n} while (((Get-Date)-$start).TotalSeconds -lt 120 -and ($t -notmatch 'Send\"?$' -or $n -eq 0 -or $t -notmatch '\\?\\\\n'))\nStart-Sleep -Seconds 6\n\"requests logged: $n\"\n& C:\\b\\wk7\\shot.ps1 -Out $Shot -Process orca-slicer\nnode C:\\b\\wk7\\cdp.mjs eval 'agent/index.html' \"document.body.innerText\"\n","numLines":24,"startLine":1,"totalLines":24}},"displayPath":"..\\..\\b\\wk7\\s42.ps1"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d1bd0a83-1d90-4656-8e58