{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"06cfc08f-7504-4961-807f-e1d5fa2ffb14","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01Fx7Uiq9RmdSEcH8PJ8T1w1","lastSequenceNum":0,"ownerAccountUuid":"7911d73c-5552-4877-a943-6a0eba3d7c4d","ownerOrganizationUuid":"68a648b0-98a4-49c7-902b-ff471f8d1d46"}
{"parentUuid":"36df6f99-b7b7-42bb-98b6-8cd5a65775e4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cge1mgzm9gnJjBAC55Gfd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The chat does look fine, and it's honest about what it changed. The problem is in the G-code, not the wording: I checked the file your slice produced, and the app generated it as if the A1 mini weren't a Bambu printer.\n\n**Your run did the same thing as mine.** You only confirmed the printer, and the model then added `G92 E0` to Before layer change G-code and sliced without asking. It told you about the change, which is good. That \"no warnings or errors\" result exists only because of that edit.\n\n**What's different in your G-code:**\n\n| | Your slice | What the code does for a Bambu printer |\n|---|---|---|\n| End-of-print `M981 S0` | missing | always writes it; the code comment says the camera uses it to know the last layer finished |\n| Start-of-print `M981 S1` (spaghetti detector) | missing | writes it on prints with normal start G-code |\n| Layer height comment | `;Z:` | `; Z_HEIGHT:` |\n| Sending to the printer | the app doesn't count it as a Bambu printer | uses the Bambu connection, unless the printer is set to use a print host |\n\nThe Bambu start and end G-code, the filament start G-code, and the layer-progress commands are all there, so this isn't garbage. It may well print.\n\n**The plate is also different.** Your slice is set for the Smooth High Temp plate, but the file asks for Textured PEI. The start G-code lowers the nozzle slightly only for Textured PEI, and your slice never runs that command. So if you use the Textured PEI plate the file asks for, without changing the setting, that adjustment is skipped. The reply does ask you to check your plate, but it doesn't know the file asked for a different one. My earlier run with the Bambu profiles installed by hand came out on Textured PEI at about 22 minutes and 4.6 g, compared with your 24 minutes and 4.8 g.\n\n**So Bug 3 is narrower than it first looked:** a new user can get a clean-looking slice by tapping yes. But they only get there because the model edited the printer's G-code, and the app still doesn't treat the printer as Bambu.\n\n**Not tested:**\n- Nothing was printed, so I don't know what a real A1 mini does without those commands.\n- I didn't press **Open the send dialog**, so the sending row comes from reading the code. I also left your open app alone.\n- The Bambu column also comes from reading the code. I have no real Bambu-mode slice to compare against, and the 3MF doesn't include one.\n\nYour test app is still open, and `C:\\b\\wk7\\ddMine` still holds a copy of the Anthropic key. Close the app and then run the `wipe-key.mjs` command I gave you earlier.\n\n**Should a Bambu file install the Bambu vendor when it's opened?** Yes means I build it and compare its G-code with your slice; no means I come back with other options for Bug 3. I recommend yes."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1760,"cache_read_input_tokens":126932,"output_tokens":951,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1760,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":951,"cache_read_input_tokens":126932,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1760,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1760},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cge1mgdSRXkvMFViQoSYz","requestRef":"c1fa21ce-29ea-4793-9b8b-a621aa92c4ac","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","attributionMcpServer":"ccd_turn","attributionMcpTool":"wrap_up","type":"